$DIR/main.p:22:7: x may have been moved at line 19, so it cannot be used here
    Thing is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when
    they are dropped. x is moved out by the type assertion x.(owned[Buf]) at
    line 19 on some paths to this point and not on others. On those paths x
    holds nothing afterwards, and the compiler cannot let a value be used where
    it may already belong to someone else.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Use x before line 19, or give it a new value on the path that moves it:
        x = ...
    Or test the ok result of the assertion at line 19 directly: where it is
    false, x still holds its value:
        if !ok {
            // use x
        }
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3302" for a longer explanation)

